ngary</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Black Army was the standing mercenary army of King Matthias Corvinus of Hungary, built up from the 1460s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/black-brunswickers"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/black-brunswickers.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Black Brunswickers</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Black Brunswickers were a volunteer corps raised in 1809 by Frederick William, Duke of Brunswick, to fight Napoleon after his duchy had been absorbed into the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/black-consciousness-movement"><span class="enc-name">Black Consciousness Movement</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Black Consciousness Movement was a South African anti-apartheid movement of the late 1960s and 1970s led by Steve Biko and others, beginning with the South African…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/black-death"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/black-death.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Black Death</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Black Death was the pandemic of plague that swept across Eurasia and North Africa in the mid-fourteenth century, killing a large share of the population.</span></a></li></ul>
